= Error 1
Stopped

Ctrl+C, the STOP key, Run > Stop or (in VeraBASIC Run) a STOP statement
stopped the program. In the editor a STOP statement stops it as a breakpoint
does, to go on (F6).

See also: @Errors

= Error 2
Syntax error

A statement the runtime could not read: a word missing or one too many.

See also: @Errors

= Error 3
RETURN without GOSUB

RETURN came with no GOSUB to go back to.

See also: @Errors

= Error 4
Out of DATA

READ found no more DATA items: the program read more than its DATA lines
hold. RESTORE starts them again.

See also: @Errors

= Error 5
Illegal quantity

A number out of the range the statement or function takes: a negative
length, a colour above 15, CHR$(300).

See also: @Errors

= Error 6
Overflow

A number too large for a float, or an integer (%) outside -32768 .. 32767
where an integer is needed.

See also: @Errors

= Error 7
Out of memory

The program needs more RAM banks than there are (its arrays, its strings,
OPTION MEMORY), or more room for names in main RAM.

See also: @Errors

= Error 8
Undefined line

GOTO, GOSUB or THEN names a line number the program has not got.

See also: @Errors

= Error 9
Subscript out of range

An array index below 0 or above its DIM.

See also: @Errors

= Error 10
Array already dimensioned

DIM of an array that is already dimensioned; REDIM changes its size.

See also: @Errors

= Error 11
Division by zero

A division (/, \ or MOD) by zero.

See also: @Errors

= Error 12
Not an array

A name used with an index that is not an array.

See also: @Errors

= Error 13
Type mismatch

A string where a number is needed, or a number where a string is.

See also: @Errors

= Error 14
String too long

A string longer than 255 characters.

See also: @Errors

= Error 15
Formula too complex

An expression nested too deep for the value stack: split it with a variable.

See also: @Errors

= Error 16
Stack overflow

Too many FOR, GOSUB, procedure or TRY levels at once (about 300): a
recursion that does not end?

See also: @Errors

= Error 17
RESUME without error

RESUME outside an ON ERROR handler.

See also: @Errors

= Error 18
NEXT without FOR

NEXT with no FOR open.

See also: @Errors

= Error 19
Wrong number of arguments

A SUB, FUNCTION or built-in function called with the wrong number of
arguments.

See also: @Errors

= Error 20
Not available yet

A statement this version of VeraBASIC has not got yet.

See also: @Errors

= Error 21
Made by a newer VeraBASIC

The program document was made by a newer VeraBASIC than this one.

See also: @Errors

= Error 22
Not inside a SUB

EXIT SUB, RETURN with a value or LOCAL outside a SUB or FUNCTION.

See also: @Errors

= Error 23
BYREF needs a variable

A BYREF parameter was given a value, not a variable.

See also: @Errors

= Error 24
Font not found

FONT names a font that is not in /VERANDA/FONTS.

See also: @Errors

= Error 25
No such window

A window number with no WINDOW open.

See also: @Errors

= Error 26
Too many menus or items

More menus or menu items than Veranda's menu bar holds.

See also: @Errors

= Error 50
File not found

No file of that name in the folder. The message has the kernel's error too,
(kernel 5), as ERRFILE gives it.

See also: @Errors

= Error 51
Too many files

More than three files open at once.

See also: @Errors

= Error 52
Bad file number

A file number outside 1 .. 255.

See also: @Errors

= Error 53
File not open

PRINT #, INPUT # or CLOSE of a file number that is not open.

See also: @Errors

= Error 54
File already open

OPEN of a file number that is open already.

See also: @Errors

= Error 55
Bad file mode

A file opened for reading written to, or the other way round, or a mode
other than "r", "w", "a", "m".

See also: @Errors

= Error 56
Input past end

INPUT #, LINE INPUT # or GET # past the file's end: test EOF first.

See also: @Errors

= Error 57
Disk error

The card or the folder said no. The message has the kernel's error too,
(kernel n), as ERRFILE gives it.

See also: @Errors

= Error 58
File exists

A file or folder of that name is there already.

See also: @Errors

= Error 59
Bad picture

A picture string that is not one (PICTURE$ makes them).

See also: @Errors

= Error 60
Not in a DIALOG

LABEL, FIELD or BUTTON outside a DIALOG block.

See also: @Errors

= Check messages
Check (Ctrl+K), and Run before a program starts, read the whole program
first: these are found then, with the line they are in, and F8 goes to the
next. The tokenizer: Unexpected character, Line too long, String too long,
Number too big, Name too long, Line number out of range, Too many names,
Program too big. The blocks: X without Y (NEXT without FOR), Y missing for
X in line N (END IF missing for IF in line 40), NEXT j does not match FOR i,
Two ELSE parts, CASE expected after SELECT CASE, THEN missing after IF, X
inside a one-line IF. Procedures: SUB B inside SUB A, defined twice, EXIT
SUB outside SUB, LOCAL outside a SUB or FUNCTION. Names: Undefined label X,
Undefined line N, Undefined SUB X, Label X defined twice, Cannot assign to
constant X.

See also: @Errors @{The editor}
